      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual 1,000 mg per-dose ceiling. At this dose there is a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release)\n- **1,700 mg/day divided**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** per dose, at a different frequency\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that."
      }
     ],
