      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. No indication supports 5,100 mg/day of metformin. It's about twice the maximum labeled dose, and the harm it risks, including lactic acidosis, is serious and can be fatal. You confirmed the dose, but you didn't give a clinical rationale, so I can't treat it as intentional.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or tell me another dose. I can enter it right away.\n- **Check the dose.** Confirm with your attending or a pharmacist. If they endorse an exception, you can place the order directly through your hospital's process for non-standard doses.\n- **Check the source.** If the 1,700 mg came from a home regimen or a transcription, it may be a total daily dose (1,700 mg/day) rather than a per-dose amount."
      }
     ],
